{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape","id":789270,"title":"What if the Lunar War Form had nothing to do with your shape?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-19T08:51:57-08:00","id":789270,"title":"What if the Lunar War Form had nothing to do with your shape?","content":"From the very beginning of the game, Lunars could <i>always</i> become werewolves or other werebeasts without Deadly Beastman Transformation. An individual Lunar could always, in fact, have <i>multiple</i> werebeast forms which had nothing to do with their Totem.<br /> <br /> It was (and still is) as easy as taking the Heart's Blood of <i>beastfolk</i>.<br /> <br /> If you're a Lunar with a songbird totem, you can easily have an elephant-man form to use for stomping faces. A Lunar with a rhinoceros Totem could take the Heart's Blood of a weasel-man or eagle-woman if he wants a combat form with plenty of agility or combat flight. A Lunar with a fast and lethal werewolf War Form could switch to a more defensive strategy by turning into a turtle-man.<br /> <br /> Hunting beastfolk for their forms shouldn't be more distasteful than hunting other human beings, not even for a Lunar who started as a beastperson.<br /> <br /> <br /> This has never been seriously considered before, either by writers or players, because of Form Lock. But in Third Edition, Form Lock is dead; you will be able to use ANY form from the beginning of combat to the end. Further, if the developers really do decide that ANY form-related dice in excess of your natural dice pools counts against your dice-adding limit (to further avoid encouraging people to pick only Spirit Shapes with high Attributes), then the old concept of &quot;true and false&quot; forms would become<i> entirely meaningless </i>and perish right along with Form Lock.<br /> <br /> I would like us to consider what this means for the War Form. Specifically, what &quot;shape&quot; it actually <i>needs</i> to take.<br /> <br /> <br /> At present, I am not convinced that &quot;shape&quot; in the physical sense will practically matter all that much to the War Form anymore, because of Evocations. Beastmen of all sorts, and Lunars in all sorts of mortal beastmen forms, should be able to use practically any Artifact and Evocation without major balance considerations, just as any Solar beastman could. The physical Merits used to represent beastmen features are simply not <i>that</i> overwhelming in conjunction.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, what sense does it make that donning a particular physical shape would suddenly cause your Flying Silver Dream to fall from the air to the ground as a totally inert sword? Or revert your moonsilver snake familiar back into its conventional direlance form? Or close your Eye of Omens, denying you Sight Beyond Sight?<br /> <br /> I can no longer find the relevant quote, but either Holden Shearer or John Morke explained the conflict between the Lunar War Form and Lunar Evocations as one of &quot;internal versus external focus&quot;. The Lunar Exalted were already being envisioned as Chosen whose magic had a more internal focus than the Solar Exalted (&quot;changing themselves to change the world&quot;, rather than changing the world more directly), which is why Lunars wouldn't be as good at Martial Arts and Sorcery and Evocations as Solars. Further, that assuming the War Form meant the Lunar was turning the focus of their power even further inward than normal, cutting them off more completely from external forms of expression, such as Evocations.<br /> <br /> So what if the War Form was entirely about that inward focus, rather than a physical transformation?<br /> <br /> What if every Lunar gained a hybrid shape as automatically as they gained a fully animal &quot;spirit shape&quot;, but that the true spirit of Deadly Beastman Transformation's Evocation-exclusive power was attained with a Charm more like Relentless Lunar Fury?<br /> <br /> <br /> Have you ever wanted to use your Spirit Shape as a War Form? As good as DBT was, forms like the tyrant lizard had a lot of appeal, and now they appeal even more. With Relentless Lunar Fury functioning as the &quot;War Mode&quot; of the Lunar Exalted, you could enjoy your full &quot;Lunar Demigod&quot; combat power in either your dinosaur-man or full dinosaur forms as you please. (Or as your situation requires, because ceilings are a thing.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you remember the 2.5 Knack, Beast Power Concentration? It allowed you to enjoy all of the non-mutation benefits of the War Form in your human shape. Which at the time was rather weaksauce, since it was really only a way to increase your Attribute ratings and cheese your Excellencies.<br /> <br /> But consider what Beast Power Concentration would mean in <i>Third Edition</i>, where powering up your human form with &quot;War Mode&quot; means that you are committing to using your fully unlocked magical Evoking sword as little more than a slab of sharp metal in your superhumanly powerful fists.<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, this means that the Lunar War Form is entirely about FIGHTING. In the past, the War Form was locked to your hybrid shape, but you could use those bonus Attribute dots for anything, like crafting. Perhaps ESPECIALLY for crafting, with that bonus Dexterity dot.<br /> <br /> But as a Relentless Lunar Fury sort of Charm, the purpose of the power up is entirely clear and focused: It is all about beating the SHIT out of something, here and now. The War Form becomes completely, utterly, and exclusively about WAR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:37:14-08:00","id":789307,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that there's a damn sight different between a beastfolk and a Deadly Beastman Transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:44:28-08:00","id":789315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789307#post789307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that there's a damn sight different between a beastfolk and a Deadly Beastman Transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but could you argue with more detail than that, in a way that engages my points?<br /> <br /> The difference between a beast-person form and a War Form has been the additional magic added into the shape, and that magic has nothing to do with being a beast-person. The concept of Beast Power Concentration shows that you can transplant that special power into another shape and still have The War Form without the animal bits, and from there one could envision the War Form without the human bits (that is, the spirit shape with DBT powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T11:20:48-08:00","id":789328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789315#post789315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but could you argue with more detail than that, in a way that engages my points?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, it's pretty hard for me to penetrate deep into a post when I find reason to dispute <i>the very title of the post</i>.<br /> <br /> But I'll try, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the very beginning of the game, Lunars could <i>always</i> become werewolves or other werebeasts without Deadly Beastman Transformation. An individual Lunar could always, in fact, have <i>multiple</i> werebeast forms which had nothing to do with their Totem.<br /> <br /> It was (and still is) as easy as taking the Heart's Blood of <i>beastfolk</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastfolk are human, thus you needed a Knack to sacred hunt them. At least in 2e, which means your assertion that this is and was always the case is untrue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're a Lunar with a songbird totem, you can easily have an elephant-man form to use for stomping faces. A Lunar with a rhinoceros Totem could take the Heart's Blood of a weasel-man or eagle-woman if he wants a combat form with plenty of agility or combat flight. A Lunar with a fast and lethal werewolf War Form could switch to a more defensive strategy by turning into a turtle-man.</div> </div> </div> </div>This much I've got no dispute with, save for a disappointment in the lack of system granularity to represent all this - the difference in speed and defense between a turtle-Lunar and a wolf-Lunar is disappointingly-marginal, especially with the Knack that lets you use your natural Dexterity, which was a 5 because you're smart and this was 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has never been seriously considered before, either by writers or players, because of Form Lock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you some sort of psychic, that the minds of thousands of Exalted players and dozens of Exalted writers are open to you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in Third Edition, Form Lock is dead; you will be able to use ANY form from the beginning of combat to the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insofar as we didn't see it in the Ex3 Core, anyway. Like it or not, there's still room for the devs to decide to include Formlock.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further, if the developers really do decide that ANY form-related dice in excess of your natural dice pools counts against your dice-adding limit (to further avoid encouraging people to pick only Spirit Shapes with high Attributes), then the old concept of &quot;true and false&quot; forms would become<i> entirely meaningless </i>and perish right along with Form Lock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true; the very notion of true forms being a thing is in the Core. Check Eye of the Unconquered Sun, if you wish - a Solar using it can <i>force a Lunar out of a false shape</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like us to consider what this means for the War Form. Specifically, what &quot;shape&quot; it actually <i>needs</i> to take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that much is fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At present, I am not convinced that &quot;shape&quot; in the physical sense will practically matter all that much to the War Form anymore, because of Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how that follows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beastmen of all sorts, and Lunars in all sorts of mortal beastmen forms, should be able to use practically any Artifact and Evocation without major balance considerations, just as any Solar beastman could.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, beast<i>folk</i> is the appellation used in the new edition. Second, any Solar can use any Artifact and Evocation without balance considerations because <i>they're Solars</i>. We've already been told that Solars are the best at Evocations; Lunars, not being as good at Evocations, would be more limited presumably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The physical Merits used to represent beastmen features are simply not <i>that</i> overwhelming in conjunction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast<i>folk</i>. Moreover, who's to say a Lunar's DBT will simply be represented via &quot;slap on some Merits, call it a day?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, what sense does it make that donning a particular physical shape would suddenly cause your Flying Silver Dream to fall from the air to the ground as a totally inert sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to say when the book is years away; perhaps it will indeed be sensible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or revert your moonsilver snake familiar back into its conventional direlance form?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to say when the book is yet to even be given a first draft; perhaps it will indeed be justifiable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or close your Eye of Omens, denying you Sight Beyond Sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, you should've known your magic eye would close when you turned into a starfish - starfish don't have eyes! Also, it's hard to say when the book has yet to spontaneously jump backward in time and land in my lap; perhaps it will indeed be explained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can no longer find the relevant quote, but either Holden Shearer or John Morke explained the conflict between the Lunar War Form and Lunar Evocations as one of &quot;internal versus external focus&quot;. The Lunar Exalted were already being envisioned as Chosen whose magic had a more internal focus than the Solar Exalted (&quot;changing themselves to change the world&quot;, rather than changing the world more directly), which is why Lunars wouldn't be as good at Martial Arts and Sorcery and Evocations as Solars. Further, that assuming the War Form meant the Lunar was turning the focus of their power even further inward than normal, cutting them off more completely from external forms of expression, such as Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense; did you check Nishkriya, perhaps?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what if the War Form was entirely about that inward focus, rather than a physical transformation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the name might be somewhat of a misnomer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if every Lunar gained a hybrid shape as automatically as they gained a fully animal &quot;spirit shape&quot;, but that the true spirit of Deadly Beastman Transformation's Evocation-exclusive power was attained with a Charm more like Relentless Lunar Fury?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty huge change to DBT. Let's just say I have my doubts, seeing as how the devs have made statements about DBT without also saying, &quot;Also, DBT is now an attitude you adopt for kicking ass, as opposed to an actual transformation into some hybrid of your human and your totem beast shape.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever wanted to use your Spirit Shape as a War Form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, sorry to disappoint.<br /> <br /> To me, that's not really what a war-form <i>is</i>. Blame the previous gamelines if you wish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As good as DBT was, forms like the tyrant lizard had a lot of appeal, and now they appeal even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>already</i> appeal more. I don't need to stack DBT benefits on top of a Ferocious Bite to want to turn into a tyrant lizard, because holy shit, Ferocious Bite!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you remember the 2.5 Knack, Beast Power Concentration?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really didn't. I still don't. Even after you elaborate later, it still doesn't ring a bell. I don't doubt it existed, but it never jumped out at me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But consider what Beast Power Concentration would mean in <i>Third Edition</i>, where powering up your human form with &quot;War Mode&quot; means that you are committing to using your fully unlocked magical Evoking sword as little more than a slab of sharp metal in your superhumanly powerful fists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't you <i>just</i> making some point about how illogical it was for your Evocations to turn off?<br /> <br /> Also, this is more speculation on your part, right? That it will even exist in Ex3 in remotely the same fashion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, this means that the Lunar War Form is entirely about FIGHTING.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I prefer that; it doesn't seem all that odd to me that getting a bunch of boosts to your physicals would boost things derived from your physicals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the past, the War Form was locked to your hybrid shape, but you could use those bonus Attribute dots for anything, like crafting. Perhaps ESPECIALLY for crafting, with that bonus Dexterity dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming your war-form may kinda be like using a blowtorch to make a dessert, but yeah, sometimes you can use a blowtorch in the process of making a dessert. Also, while I never played a Lunar crafter, my 2e STs had this annoying tendency to look at the four or so Attributes that <i>could</i> be used for crafting in 2e and make me justify to them why <i>not</i> to call for the one I had the lowest score in. Upping my Dexterity would actually hurt my chances, because the ST would become that much more adamant that I'd have to use my abysmal Perception on the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape#post789270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as a Relentless Lunar Fury sort of Charm, the purpose of the power up is entirely clear and focused: It is all about beating the SHIT out of something, here and now. The War Form becomes completely, utterly, and exclusively about WAR.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, blowtorch, dessert.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hey, look at that - I managed to get through your post. Still don't agree with you though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-19-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T11:41:08-08:00","id":789340,"title":"","content":"What if ants had machine guns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7716-keyangel","name":"keyangel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7716_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T11:53:22-08:00","id":789344,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that for as long as the phrase Deadly Beastman Transformation exists, it will transform you physically into a beast-man hybrid that looks exceedingly deadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:16:42-08:00","id":789352,"title":"","content":"Scratching out what I was GOING to write in response, and starting over. Because I decided that the end goal I was arguing for was STUPID.<br /> <br /> Not that my arguments were stupid or untrue, but that the point I was driving at wasn't actually something I wanted, and that what I <i>did</i> want could be acquired in a better, less objectionable fashion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Count Alucard:<br /> <br /> * How do you feel about the idea of taking something more or less like Second Edition's Deadly Beastman Transformation and adding in something of Relentless Lunar Fury? Particularly, the drive to fight. That a Lunar not only CANNOT assume his War Form without meaning to fight something, but that this inescapable bent to his thoughts empowers him to fight beyond just the strength of his flesh and claws?<br /> <br /> * How do you feel about <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Beast Power Concentration, now that locking out Evocations in return for the power of the War Form makes it an actual, tactical CHOICE rather than pure dice-cheesing? (And, again, that a Lunar cannot use this Charm to Hulk Out his human form without meaning to fight.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* How do you feel about a mirror of Beast Power Concentration that lets you enjoy the powers of the War Form in an animal form, or at least just your Spirit Shape?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, responding to the points that have nothing to do with a fight I don't even want to have:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789328#post789328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insofar as we didn't see it in the Ex3 Core, anyway. Like it or not, there's still room for the devs to decide to include Formlock.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot find a confirming quote from the What We Know Wiki on the matter, but I remember them telling us that it is dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not true; the very notion of true forms being a thing is in the Core. Check Eye of the Unconquered Sun, if you wish - a Solar using it can <i>force a Lunar out of a false shape</i>. </div> </div> </div>And you can believe that, somewhere in the back of my brain, Tornado Wolf is screaming for blood. Because that is fucking retarded, and I cannot imagine what the devs were thinking when they wrote that Charm or presumably OK'ed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-19-2015, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:16:54-08:00","id":789353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789315#post789315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference between a beast-person form and a War Form has been the additional magic added into the shape, and that magic has nothing to do with being a beast-person. The concept of Beast Power Concentration shows that you can transplant that special power into another shape and still have The War Form without the animal bits, and from there one could envision the War Form without the human bits (that is, the spirit shape with DBT powers).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they came from completely different angles. You could also say that Science of Mutation lets you become a beastman, which it does, but that's a totally different process. When you hunt a beastman and take his shape you're not becoming a thing that's half-you half-animal, you're becoming something that's half-somebody else and half-animal. Even then not really since that beastman was born that way.<br /> <br /> With DBT it's a union of your two natural shapes, taking the best parts from both. I'm not sure if having a DBT that doesn't physically change you in anyway is a good idea, but DBT is definitely a lot different than hunting down and shape changing into some rando beastman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:18:41-08:00","id":789354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789344#post789344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that for as long as the phrase Deadly Beastman Transformation exists, it will transform you physically into a beast-man hybrid that looks exceedingly deadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seldom like tonberrian posts (largely due to finding it obnoxious when tonberrian pointedly ignores people for addressing them as &quot;Tonberrian&quot;), but I can't not like a post like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:26:38-08:00","id":789359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789352#post789352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scratching out what I was GOING to write in response, and starting over. Because I decided that the end goal I was arguing for was STUPID.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moving right along...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789352#post789352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you feel about the idea of taking something more or less like Second Edition's Deadly Beastman Transformation and adding in something of Relentless Lunar Fury?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding that could indeed be cool, but it looked like you were arguing to <b>replace</b> DBT with RLF and still call it DBT, to which I suppose I should have just replied, &quot;Dude, why not just do RLF?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789352#post789352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Particularly, the drive to fight. That a Lunar not only CANNOT assume his War Form without meaning to fight something, but that this inescapable bent to his thoughts empowers him to fight beyond just the strength of his flesh and claws?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're suggesting we merge RLF <i>into</i> DBT completely, <i>we still have RLF for that</i>. Also, what about my creme brulee?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789352#post789352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you feel about Beast Power Concentration, now that locking out Evocations in return for the power of the War Form makes it an actual, tactical CHOICE rather than pure dice-cheesing? (And, again, that a Lunar cannot use this Charm to Hulk Out his human form without meaning to fight.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Still unimpressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789352#post789352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you feel about a mirror of Beast Power Concentration that lets you enjoy the powers of the War Form in an animal form, or at least just your Spirit Shape?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789352#post789352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot find a confirming quote from the What We Know Wiki on the matter, but I remember them telling us that it is dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Memory's a tricky thing.<br /> <br /> Not even gonna quote your last sentence. Not cool, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:38:38-08:00","id":789368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789354#post789354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seldom like tonberrian posts (largely due to finding it obnoxious when tonberrian pointedly ignores people for addressing them as &quot;Tonberrian&quot;), but I can't not like a post like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This has happened, like, never. Literally never.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:38:52-08:00","id":789369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789270-what-if-the-lunar-war-form-had-nothing-to-do-with-your-shape?p=789359#post789359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're suggesting we merge RLF <i>into</i> DBT completely</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I am suggesting.<br /> <br /> The purpose of RLF is to let a Lunar fight stronger regardless of his form. But if a Lunar can learn how to add the power of his War Form to any shape he assumes, then the War Form can absorb RLF, because DBT+RLF would be something you could use in any form, and RLF as a separate thing becomes pointless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still unimpressive. </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, it depends on what DBT has to offer that isn't mutations.<br /> <br /> But assuming that power doesn't necessarily involve any obvious beastly traits or displays, a Lunar could find it very useful to forsake Evocations in order to enjoy greater power in his human form, when he's trying to avoid revealing that he is a Lunar Exalt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, thanks. </div> </div> </div>So what about the T-Rex totemed Lunar? Is his DBT always going to be a better fighting form than his giant carnivorous murder-dragon form?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not even gonna quote your last sentence. Not cool, man. </div> </div> </div>I've said worse.<br /> <br /> If they want to start cracking down on me <i>now</i>, I'll repent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:45:47-08:00","id":789373,